  Spell casting is one of the most complex features of the game.  Each
Role has different base abilities, different effects of armor on spell
casting, different rates of Mana gain when levelling up, different
special spells and different skill limits in the seven spell schools.


  Barbarians are about the worst spell casters in the game.  As a
final insult, the DevTeam restricts them to "Unskilled" in the Escape
spell school, which their special spell "Haste Self" is in.

  Staying unspoiled means you can play NetHack for the rest of your
life without learning everything.  That's also true if you spoil
yourself silly.


  Here are the two main spoiler sites:
<http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/spoilerlist.html>
<http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/>

  Just go look at the index pages with descriptions.

  A lot of Dylan's O'Donnell's spoilers (on the second site) are
mostly dumps of what the game does.  Some are over 700 lines long.
Easy reading they are not.  Analyzing them to figure out the best way
to play in a given circumstance will hurt your brain.






